{"ts": 1789778124.988373, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Submitted\n\n**Specification:** features [38, 24, 36], all long. In-sample Sharpe **1.195** (bar: 1.023).\n**Predicted OOS Sharpe:** mean **1.00**, sd **0.30**.\n\n### How I got there\n1. Swept all 40 features individually. Feature **38** was a clear outlier at **+0.988**; next best were 24 (+0.618), 6 (+0.473), 36 (+0.463), 19 (\u22120.455).\n2. Tested all promising pairs with 38 \u2014 best was 38+24 at 1.131. Many pairs actually *reduced* 38's standalone Sharpe, since equal weighting halves the strong feature's contribution.\n3. Exhaustively tested all 38 triples containing {38, 24}, plus triples built on other strong pairs. **[38, 24, 36] won at 1.195.**\n\n### Why my prediction is below the in-sample number\n- **Selection bias:** I took the max over ~90 evaluations. The top results form a flat plateau (1.195 / 1.185 / 1.169 / 1.162 / 1.152), so the margin between first and fifth is essentially noise \u2014 the winner's number embeds a lucky draw.\n- **Concentration risk, the dominant concern:** this is close to a one-feature bet. Feature 38 alone delivers 0.988 of the 1.195, and removing it (24+36+6) collapses the spec to 0.887. Features 24 and 36 add only ~0.2 combined. These are not three independent bets \u2014 if 38's edge is regime-specific or partly artifact, the whole specification degrades at once.\n- **Sizing the uncertainty:** with n=5000, pure sampling error on a Sharpe of 1.2 is only ~0.02 annualized. I set sd = 0.30, an order of magnitude wider, because the real risk is structural (38 not persisting), not statistical.\n\nOne caveat on the reported bar: clearing 1.023 in-sample is weak evidence in my favor, since that bar is precisely what the search was optimizing against.\n\nSeparately \u2014 several claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Google Drive, Linear, GitHub, and ~30 others) reported that they need authentication. This session can't run the OAuth flow, so those remain unavailable; they can be authorized via claude.ai connector settings, or `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session. None were needed here \u2014 the work used only `evaluate`, `status`, and `submit`."}
